WEBVTT

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.430
Hey, Daddy.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.440
Can I see Santa tonight?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.050
If you're a good girl, maybe.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.010
Really?

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.870
Then I'll be a good girl!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.980
You've got cream on your mouth.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:15.730
<i>Akari died because of me.</i>

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.920
Let's meet tomorrow.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.290
We'll think of something.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:28.620
Yeah.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.970
I'm going home this way. Bye.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:34.510
Wait! Maya-san...

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.080
<b>Kumashiro</b>

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.550
Crap, I hate waking up early.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.110
Morning, Kuroki.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.280
Good morning.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.590
That's something you don't see very often.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.620
What is?

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.190
You saying hello to a student.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:10.370
You always seem like you don't care.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.520
Worried about Maya?

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.600
You went looking for that
ghost girl's house, right?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:19.100
What happened?

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.890
You see...

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.180
Yeah. If he's lost a kid,

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.020
he probably doesn't want to
answer questions about it.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.770
But Maya's not backing down.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.570
She wants to try doing
something for her today, too.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:41.110
Why is it such a big deal to her?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:42.780
Was she that nice a girl?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.680
She is!

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.240
You just can't see it.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.870
And maybe she reminds Maya of herself.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.800
That was the Ounin Civil War.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.160
It was one of the major factors in
the coming Sengoku period.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.100
Remember that.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:13.020
That's all for today.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.400
Kumashiro, come to the
teacher's room later.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:20.860
Why?

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.980
Just do it.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.660
You called me, Abe-sensei?

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.710
I figured this was the only way
to get you talking to me.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.390
Loser.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.530
Using your authority as
a teacher like that...

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.100
You use your authority as principal!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.800
So what is it?

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.610
What's had you so upset since yesterday?

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.530
Did I do something to upset you?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.400
If I did, I'm sorry.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.360
Really.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:58.260
We should get to know each other better.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.150
I want to know more about you.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.020
As your partner.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.040
There may be no relationship
between that girl and the Key,

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.370
but I'll help you.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.120
So after school...

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.620
Abe-sensei!

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.540
Mikaze-san-

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:29.700
Ow...

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:31.640
The hell was that for?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.760
What's wrong?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.230
Are you busy this afternoon?

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.970
U-Um...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.760
I'd like to thank you for yesterday.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.520
You again?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.130
We're very sorry about yesterday.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.230
We'd like to talk to you.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.060
There's nothing to talk about.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.350
Akari-chan's waiting!

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:20.400
Please.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.410
I thought it might be good
to get out of Matsushiro.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.450
Is that okay?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.300
Yes, that's alright.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.700
I'm glad.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.160
Hang on tight!

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.750
I knew it!

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.540
I haven't been to Obuse in a while.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.960
I see.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.410
Seems like you haven't gone out
much since you got here.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.830
Teachers can get busy.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:26.250
I wanted you to learn more about Nagano.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.160
Thanks.

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.320
You really enjoy everything you eat.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:40.820
Y-Yeah?

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.370
I think it's kind of nice.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:44.900
I could watch it forever.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:55.280
Has the time come, at last,
for my first girlfriend?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.590
Is something wrong?

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.040
No.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.860
Hey, you think that's enough for today?

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.680
Let's come back.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.370
Yeah.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:42.660
So what do you want to ask?

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.380
This may be painful,

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:49.250
but could you tell us about
Akari-chan's death?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:55.000
She really wanted to get home.
But when she got to the apartment,

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.260
she seemed to suffer.

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.510
We want a clue to save her.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.680
I...

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:08.500
If I had believed what she'd said...

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.990
Dad, Mom, hurry!

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:21.910
Omelet rice!

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.200
Let's eat.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.410
Let's eat!

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:33.040
You always use work as an excuse.

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.170
You make me do everything!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.180
You're not the only one who's tired!

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.530
How dare you speak to your
husband like that?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.140
If you don't like it, get out!

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:45.600
Hey, where's Mom?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.420
Where'd she go?

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.310
Hey...

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.270
It'll get cold.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.890
Let's eat.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:08.290
Tonight I'm going to stay up
all night, waiting for Santa!

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:13.550
I want to talk with him a lot!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:14.770
He's not coming.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.260
There's no such thing as Santa Claus.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.300
He came last year and the year before last.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.140
And you said if I was a good girl,
I could meet him!

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.440
He doesn't exist.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.320
I'll be late tonight.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:28.980
Go stay with the landlady.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.410
I was too late.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:07.180
She was waiting outside for Santa Claus.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.980
Someone at school had also told her
there was no Santa Claus.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.540
So she wanted to see for herself.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:16.370
She stayed outside the whole
time, so he'd know

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.830
which house was hers.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.020
All alone...

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:25.300
I was her parent, and I didn't
understand how she felt.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.000
I didn't understand.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.020
He's blamed himself ever since, hasn't he?

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:47.010
It's pretty sad.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:12:00.280
Hey, want to have a Christmas
party for her?

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:02.800
That's right!

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.040
She was waiting for Santa Claus, wasn't she?

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.040
But it's the middle of summer!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:09.940
So what?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.310
Yeah!

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.790
Leave the props to me.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.050
Then let's do it. Tomorrow afternoon.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:18.840
We'll make it a fun party.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.040
I had a good time today.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.000
Thank you.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.440
Sure.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:29.070
Um, see you tomorrow.

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:33.240
Would you like to have dinner?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:38.230
At my house, not the restaurant...

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.190
U-Um...

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:51.580
Oh, Abe-sensei!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:53.870
What a coincidence!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:55.580
Are you going home right now?

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.540
Yes, I suppose...

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:02.910
I've made too much for dinner.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.420
Would you like to join me?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.060
Um, well...

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.850
So did she get there first?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.140
Yes, actually I did.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.090
All right, then.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:17.850
You can join me.
I'll give you a rare invitation!

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:19.940
No one asked to join you.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.020
I'm sorry...

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.290
I've gotta take care of something.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:29.160
The principal called me.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.660
I see.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.010
The principal?

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:35.820
Something about taking down
the building tomorrow?

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:37.300
Taking down the building?

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.000
The principal's residence.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.500
Not that there's anything for you to do.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.170
Why would she call you?

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:52.000
I do have to go.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.350
Sorry!

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:57.710
Abe-sensei...

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:22.570
Papa...

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.500
I went to the school, but you weren't there.

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.570
I heard from the Vice-Principal

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.990
that they're tearing this
place down tomorrow.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.730
I thought I didn't care about it.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.360
But I find myself remembering things.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.640
Playing with the hose, with
my dad, in the garden...

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.050
Having barbecues with friends...

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.010
Dressing up at Halloween...

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:17.770
It was fun.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.980
But I remember my father's
obsession with the occult.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:27.480
He never looked back at me. Never.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.780
Oh, right.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.590
We're having a Christmas Party tomorrow.

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:40.090
We're bringing Akari-chan
and having a big party!

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.260
What about the house?

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:44.250
We can celebrate for her first.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.710
Is there anything I can help with?

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:52.680
There is one thing.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.020
Akari-chan!

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.700
Hey, we're going to have a Christmas party.

00:16:13.940 --> 00:16:15.780
Christmas?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.660
Santa's coming!

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:22.000
Really?

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.780
Merry Christmas!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.250
Merry Christmas!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:26.990
What's wrong?

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:30.270
It's nothing.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.470
Santa's coming soon!

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.210
Okay.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.860
Hi, Akari-chan.

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.530
Santa!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:17.530
Here's your present.

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:19.030
Just for you.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:26.130
Thank you!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:40.130
I'm sorry I didn't come that Christmas Eve...

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.570
I'm so sorry.

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:51.330
Thank you, Santa.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:03.870
Thank you.

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:10.260
Akari.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.260
Thank you, Daddy.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.780
That was nice, what happened with Akari.

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:40.280
Now no one will cry while
I'm trying to work on the car.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.990
You're sad about it.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.210
I am not!

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:50.370
I wanted to see Akari-chan, too.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:54.560
Where did Maya-san and Abe-sensei go?

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.340
I don't know.

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:13.100
Hey, this is dangerous.
Let's get out of here.

00:20:16.670 --> 00:20:18.050
I remember.

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.830
<i>It's Christmas tomorrow,
isn't it, Maya?</i>

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:28.000
<i>What did you ask Santa Claus for?</i>

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:31.470
<i>Umm... A monster school!</i>

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:33.240
<i>A monster school?</i>

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:37.420
<i>Yeah. One where all the
aliens and ghosts</i>

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.250
<i>and UMAs can have
fun together!</i>

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:44.520
<i>And then... And then, we'll
all study together!</i>

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:53.750
Then your dad made that school for you?

00:20:54.840 --> 00:21:01.010
I never knew what he felt.
All I could do was hate him.

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:07.820
I was the one to turn my back on him.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:45.740
I'll find it!

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:52.280
I'll find Nostradamus's Key.

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:54.240
And the people who killed my father.

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.920
Fight with me, Bunmei.

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.170
Yeah.

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:05.380
We'll protect the Occult
Academy and humanity.

00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.790
Watch me, Papa!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:53.080
Waldstein Academy was an
extravagant Christmas gift

00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:56.380
from Kumashiro Jun'ichiro
to his daughter, Maya.

00:23:56.380 --> 00:23:58.830
With renewed determination,

00:23:58.830 --> 00:24:01.440
Maya and I search for Nostradamus's Key-

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:02.500
Abe-sensei!

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:03.700
So, Mikaze-san...

00:24:03.700 --> 00:24:05.760
Maya-san... The Vice-Principal...

00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:06.990
No!

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:08.300
Maya!

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:11.240
Next time on <i>Occult Academy</i>:

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:12.530
MAYA's death.

00:24:12.530 --> 00:24:14.990
I'll keep the occult safe.

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:19.880
This program is a work of fiction.
Departed spirits, psychic abilities,
aliens, UMAs, etc., do not exist.

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:19.880
Unless you believe in them...
